WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.660
Before you start studying,

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.760
make sure you've got everything you need.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.720
On your table should be class notes, the syllabus,

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:10.660
required books, teachers slides, the tools you need,

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:13.320
and ideally examples of previous exams

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:16.000
so you know the structure and how it'll be graded.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.620
In your fridge there should be superfoods:

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:22.660
almonds, fruits, veggies and yogurt should do the job.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.180
Even if your brain's weight

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.700
is only around 2% of your body weight,

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.680
it uses up around 20% of its energy.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.720
To avoid procrastination,

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.540
shut down all distractions

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.760
and tell your friends not to disturb.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.820
Ideally you should start studying weeks before,

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.140
but lets assume that you have just 7 days

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.140
and 3 hours a day.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:47.560
On day 1, your aim is to get context,

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.220
to see the big picture.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:52.940
This is important, because context
acts like a memory network,

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.580
to which you can attach all details.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:59.740
First you make connections and then later
remember things easier.

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:02.440
To get there fast, read the class syllabus,

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:05.380
skim through text-books and review all the materials

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:07.140
without going into details.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:09.080
If you're studying roman history,

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:12.120
watch an epic movie about Caesar in the evening.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.880
If its physics, go visit a science museum

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:17.240
and try to understand whats going on.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:19.060
Once you see the big picture,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:21.120
chunk it up and make a plan.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:22.980
If there are 10 chapters to learn

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:27.340
and 5 days to do that, cover 2 chapters each day.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:29.900
Day 2.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:33.720
Now it's cramming time and you have to 
learn 2 chapters.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:37.820
To study effectively, make handwritten notes
in your own language.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:41.940
Even better, try to explain it in your own
simple words out loud

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:43.800
to check your understanding.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:48.660
Every 30-45 minutes or so, take a short 5-10
minute break.

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:52.380
That will maximize your retention and
keep creativity up.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:55.040
Also keep snacking on nuts and fruits

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:57.080
to boost your brain's energy.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.640
Finish your session with an instant self-test

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.300
to check your understanding.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:05.960
Such quick tests can improve retention by up to 30%.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.480
Day 3 to 6.

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:11.780
Start by reviewing your own summaries

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:14.280
and the material from the previous days.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.380
Look at your instant self-test

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:19.160
and check what you got right and what you got wrong.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:21.320
Where there are gaps, fill them.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:22.920
As you have 3 hours,

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:24.840
spend 1 hour on that review

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:28.320
and 2 hours learning the next chapters
of the material.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:30.900
Like the days before: start reading,

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.860
take notes, summarize in your own words

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:36.180
and then finish with a self-test.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:38.960
Day 7.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.940
Again, start by reviewing yesterday’s work.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.640
Then spend the remaining time

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:45.960
reviewing everything one more time:

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:47.720
all 10 chapters.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:49.160
To check your understanding,

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:51.060
you can use the table of contents,

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.340
which is like a very short summary of the entire book.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.620
If you have time left, write an essay to summarize

00:02:57.620 --> 00:02:59.960
all the materials into one big chunk

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:02.020
or do a full test-exam.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:04.280
In the evening, pack your bag

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:06.620
and everything you need for the exam day.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.560
Then go to bed early.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.380
Good sleep before the test

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:13.060
can increase your performance by 30%

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:16.340
- dreams are essential in remembering.

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:18.900
Exam Day.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:21.320
Get up on time, so you don't start the day

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.940
already completely stressed out.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:27.820
Begin your day by eating a good breakfast

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:31.200
to give your brain the energy to run for the next hours.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:34.500
Research suggests high-carb, high-fiber,

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:38.060
slow-digesting foods like oats or brown rice.

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:40.060
Then leave home on time

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:43.780
so you arrive at the exam room on time
without being in a rush.

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:47.540
Stress mixes up your hormones and should be avoided.

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:50.680
Once you sit in the test,

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:52.220
skim over all questions

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:54.340
so you get an idea of what’s on it.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:58.220
Then try to see how each question
relates to each other.

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:00.380
When you realize how each question

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:03.060
connects to the next or to the big picture,

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:06.500
you will have a higher recall and find betters answers.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:08.940
If you are afraid you might run out of time,

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:10.820
do some quick math to figure out

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:13.280
how much time you have for each question.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:14.880
Then start.

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:18.380
Carefully read the question.

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:21.200
You get more points for answering a question poorly

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.200
than writing the perfect answer that's off topic.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.220
If a question is too hard,

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:29.160
skip it first and go straight for the easy ones.

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.700
While collecting points for easy questions,

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:34.940
our brain can subconsciously work
on the harder questions

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:37.000
and an answer might pop up.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.600
If you get too stressed,

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:42.000
take a short break and a couple of long deep breaths.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.860
This gets your brain back into thinking mode.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:46.880
If you're doing a multiple choice question

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:49.960
and you are not sure, go with your first guess.

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:52.520
Usually, your first instinct is right.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.320
If you have NO idea at all

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:56.580
but there is no punishment for being wrong,

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:58.860
then just guess anything quickly.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.400
In the end, if you still have time left,

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:05.000
use it to review your answers or correct your spelling.

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:09.900
For more tips, watch our other sprouts videos.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:11.180
If we missed something,

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:12.700
post it in the comments below

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:14.440
so we can learn from you.

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:17.220
If you have an exam soon, don't stress.

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:21.060
Even if you would fail it, it’s probably
not the end of the world.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:25.780
As Jack Ma said:
“I flunked my exam for university two times

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:30.060
before I was accepted by what was considered my city's worst university.”

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:33.540
Today he’s China’s biggest success story.

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:34.740
Good luck!

